  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q54-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "54",
    "prompt": "Find the number of terms needed to be added for the sum to exceed 1 000 000 in the series $4+16+64+\\cdots$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "10 terms.",
      "worked": "$a=4$, $r=4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&>1000000\\\\\\frac{a(r^n-1)}{r-1}&>1000000\\\\\\frac{4(4^n-1)}{4-1}&>1000000\\\\4^n-1&>750000\\\\4^n&>750001\\\\n&>\\log_4 750001\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $\\log_4 750001\\approx9.76$, the least integer satisfying the inequality is $n=10$.\n\nTherefore, 10 terms are needed.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
